Id: sysd004w
Severity: WARN
Category: services
Check: check_units
Fix: chown root (or the service's user) the program and its directories, and chmod go-w them.
References: systemd.service(5)
Controls: CIS 4.1; NIST CM-5, CM-6; ISO 8.9; CE Secure configuration

An enabled systemd service runs a program (an ExecStart= or another
Exec*= line) that, or a directory above which, does not belong to the
account the service runs as (User=, root when there is none) nor to
root. Whoever owns it can replace the program, and their code then runs
as that account, at every start, which for most services is root.

It is a WARN when the program is executable, or when the service does
not run as root.

To fix it, give the program and its directories to root (or to the
service's user), take group and other write permission off them, and
keep scripts that services run in a root-owned directory such as
/usr/local/sbin.
